# Files in dist/ that must NOT be served as public static assets.
#
# wrangler.toml points `assets.directory` at the whole of dist/, which is also
# where the Cloudflare adapter writes the compiled server bundle. Without this
# file Wrangler refuses to deploy at all, and rightly so: uploading _worker.js
# as an asset would publish the server-side code on the open internet.
#
# Lives in public/ so Astro copies it into dist/ on every build — dist/ is
# generated and git-ignored, so the file cannot live there directly.
_worker.js
_routes.json
